        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/13c87172-3884-43fb-964c-6af78a968da1,1777051012638/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C98%2C1024%2C576%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='Two people talk with one another while standing between two rows of people in military attire.' width='620' height='349' title='WINDSOR, ENGLAND - SEPTEMBER 17: US President Donald Trump (R) and King Charles III (C) review the Guard of Honour after arrival at Windsor Castle on day two of the US President Donald Trump&apos;s second state visit to the UK on September 17, 2025 in Windsor, England. (Photo by Kirsty Wigglesworth - WPA Pool/Getty Images)'/><p>King Charles's state visit to the United States includes high-profile formal events such as a state dinner and a speech to the U.S. Congress. There are also events in New York City and Virginia, where he and Queen Camilla will have a chance to focus on interests and causes they often devote time to \u2014 even as the trip garners attention for the broader circumstances",
