        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/a6b583fd-9148-43d0-9723-a1fb263f655b,1777045276241/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C742%2C1080%2C607%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='A truck featuring a Love, Scarborough ad drives past the Rogers Centre.' width='620' height='349' title='The Scarborough Health Network Foundation launched the Love, Scarborough campaign in 2022. Since then, the SHN Foundation has raised more than $200 million.'/><p>As people live longer and have more complex medical needs, hospitals are turning to bolder advertising and marketing to attract top-tier professionals and afford the latest equipment in diagnostics and treatment.</p>",
